(text "TUB 1 AC ENTRY / AUTO VOLTAGE SELECT (bom 17p) - on the prereg PCB.  Sense-before-select: the transformers are TAPPED 0/115/230 V primaries; K901 de-energized feeds the 230 V ends (TAP230 = safe wiring).  The 200k/36.5k divider on the 9 VAC aux reservoir VSEL_AUX hands the LM393 ~0.155 x V_SEL; the 1.24 V TLV431 threshold = ~8.0 V aux -> 115 V mains gives ~5.5 V aux on the 230 V tap (selects TAP115), 230 V gives ~11-12 V (stays TAP230).  Wide, race-free margin for a 120/240 V service spread." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.000 20.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.50 1.50)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a2da7d2a-2a2c-4e99-a49b-4e972cf7ee57"))
(text "SEQUENCE: mains on -> reservoirs charge through R900 -> ~1.65 s TLC555 arm delay -> Q812 releases the LM393 gate node SEL_GATE -> comparator samples -> if low-line, K901 energizes (TAP115) and D817 clamps the sense node so a post-select reservoir jump cannot chatter the state -> ARMS rises and Q813 energizes the K900 bypass relay across R900." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.000 27.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "567bd3f1-fa16-43e6-a7d9-4342e9f35404"))
(text "LAYOUT NOTES: all mains-domain parts live in a fenced AC zone at the board edge by the chassis DD12 power-entry module (inlet/fuse/switch/filter are chassis-side, QC-tab feed to J900); >=6 mm creepage/clearance primary-to-SELV and L-to-N, milled slot under K901 between the primary-contact poles; MOVs + CM choke tight to the board's mains input; PE bond to the chassis screw next to the module; NO analog or digital copper inside the AC zone; transformers in a row along the AC-zone boundary with primaries facing it; aux/select logic is SELV - keep it on the secondary side of the creepage boundary." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.000 33.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.20 1.20)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f1273819-71eb-485a-a97f-121edc6a2ab1"))
